@0    = ~I understand that you were one of the law-keepers in this land before you turned renegade. The way you hold yourself suggests the warrior's training has not left you.~
@1    = ~Thanks. I try to keep myself in practice.~
@2    = ~Did you enter their service by choice, or were you placed there?~
@3    = ~Was by choice, if you count having no idea what to do with your life a choice. I had a good time there.~
@4    = ~Then you had a luxury. Consider yourself blessed.~
@5    = ~I wonder that your mother did not chastise you for your mode of speech, surfacer.~
@6    = ~Oh, she did! One time she chewed me out for telling my teacher that she should shove her books up--~
@7    = ~"Chewed you out"?~
@8    = ~Yeah - like, told me off.~
@9    = ~Tell you what, I can teach you some sayings in Common as we go. They'll come in handy!~
@10   = ~You seem to speak always with a smile on your face, Faren. I do not believe it possible, after you have lost so much.~
@11   = ~Not all the time. Maybe you've only seen me on good days.~
@12   = ~Surfacers are a curious group. You seem to shift and change, and I cannot fathom how or why.~
@13   = ~Well, you should get used to it, or you'll run into trouble.~
